Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||08-10-2000||10:19 AM||||<BR>I just Bougt a 1985 Fiero GT hardtop (no sunroof). My question is, Are hardtops rare? I only ever see Fiero's W/ sunroofs. I bought the car for $300 i horible shape but i got it because it was a hard top so I can cut T-Tops, But if it is rare I won't cut the roof.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||08-10-2000||11:03 AM||||<BR>I have or had the following:<BR>84 SC - NO sunroof<BR>84 SE - NO sunroof<BR>86 SC - NO sunroof<BR>87 SC - NO sunroof<P>85 GT - sunroof<BR>86 SE - sunroof<P>If those are indicators, I would say that hardtops are not rare.<P>Want to add one thing.<BR>When dealing with a higher trim package (like GT trim) the hardtop may be rare.  So I would find out the production numbers for the 85 GTs.<P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||08-10-2000||03:21 PM||||When you remove the plastic roof, you will find the cutout for the sunroof is already there. That whole section gets cut out for the T-top so it makes no difference if the car had a sunroof or not. <BR>Terry||||reg||1
